@* What a new password must be, under the new-password box on every screen that sets one - the invitation, reset
   password, My Account's change password (4 Nov 2026, Steve - as DavidsonHR's). The rules come from KpiIdentityRules,
   where the server's are set, so the list can't disagree with what it refuses. Each bullet becomes a green tick once the
   password in the box named by For meets it, and a bullet again if it stops (js/passwordRules.js); the tick is a
   different SHAPE, and the hidden "done" tells a screen reader. A guide only: the server still checks everything. *@
@using Kpi.Data.Auth

<div class="pw-rules" id="@Id" data-pw-rules-for="@For">
    <div>Your password must have:</div>
    <ul>
        @foreach (var rule in KpiIdentityRules.PasswordRules)
        {
            <li data-pw-check="@rule.Check">@rule.Text<span class="visually-hidden" data-pw-state></span></li>
        }
    </ul>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string? Id { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The id of the password box whose value ticks the rules off.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string For { get; set; } = "";
}
